The single skip is
`tests.test_mutations_checks.FixtureInventory.test_a_symlink_in_place_of_a_file_fails`,
which needs the Windows privilege to create a symbolic link and skips itself
rather than reporting a pass it did not earn.

    worker 0: 33 tests, 600.0s of test time
    worker 1: 11 tests, 497.2s of test time
    worker 2: 44 tests, 399.2s of test time
    worker 3: 72 tests, 575.3s of test time
    worker 4: 23 tests, 607.2s of test time

Per-worker test time sums to more than the elapsed wall clock because the
runner distributes individual test IDs, so a class fixture runs once per test
method rather than once per class. That is the cost of every test being
independently addressable and sharing no state.

## What this run covers that the last one did not

Where the placement-orientation offsets come from. The registry is no longer a
table the generator applies and the gate then reads back - which would only
prove a program can apply its own table twice. `tests/test_cpl_orientation.py`
grew to 18 tests covering the registry as an authority: that every populated
part number carries an explicit reviewed entry including the twelve at zero
offset, that each declared offset re-derives from the frozen library evidence
under `fabrication/jlc_orientation/` and matches its recorded digest, that
normalisation lands in [0, 360), that references sharing a part number are
corrected identically, and that the 36 fractional array angles survive
generation unrounded.

The regression test for the defect that started it removes `C7668` - U2's part
number - from the registry and runs the real generation code, not an edited
output: U2 must receive no angle at all and the failure must name that part.
There is no default offset, so a part nobody has reviewed cannot ship as if it
had been.

One test is sensitive to machine load rather than to the code:
`tests.test_runner.RunnerContract.test_concurrent_tests_never_share_an_output_directory`
asserts that four staggered tests reach more than one worker, which does not
hold when the machine is already saturated. It passes on an idle machine.
